;NOTE: This program is written for and compiled with Eric Isaacson's A86
;      assembly language compiler, using Options +P0 -F (8086/8088 CPU and
;      no FPU).
;==============================================================================

;Need to fix GetCallBackAddr so it returns error if we're at command-line.
;Need Single Character, Memory (String), etc. Options?
;Write {RSV} for Reserved characters, something for FEFFh, {ILG} for illegal
;  characters, ...?
;Add UTF32 Tables, but don't do anything with them?
;  Auto-Detect UTF32 based on assuming FEFFh at beginning of File?
;  UTF32 Option on command-line?
;Option to print ranges and single values, Options for memory, Redirected
;  Input, etc.
;For Reserved, Illegal, etc. Put Hex Code inside brackets along with
;  description.  Also for Controls?  Minimum characters for length (Byte, Word,
;  DWord)?
;FFFEh & FFFFh are reserved in ALL Planes.
;Do UTF-8/16/32 conversion, translate to BP:AX
;Max is 10FFFFh, not FFFF_FFFFh!
;If no BOM present, assume Big-Endian (UNICODE Spec)?
;Test String Decryption on Analog Joystik USB Adapter on old desktop -
;  it hangs and prints multiple invalid characters (most likely a problem in
;  USBUHCI).
;Need Options to display ranges, single characters, multiple ranges/characters,
;  from memory (actual characters), from file (either direct characters or
;  ASCII descriptions)).  How to handle redirected output string?
;Look for CMDLINE Env variable!
;Byte-Order-Mark (BOM) encodings:
;  UTF32BE 00 00 FE FF
;  UTF32LE FF FE 00 00
;  UTF16BE FE FF
;  UTF16LE FF FE
;  UTF8    EF BB BF
;  If encoding is unknown and there is no BOM, assume Big-Endian
;  If encoding is specifically known, BOM must NOT be used.




;In Docs:
;Only words (not DWords)
;UniCode 5.0
;Tries to display character using ASCII chars 20h-7Eh, so may not be
;  an exact (or even very close) match.  Designed to support other programs
;  of mine, so is not a comprehensive program.
;Also checks CodePage, and writes appropriate characters where it can
;  (instead of "approximating" it with true ASCII).
;  Could be expanded later to handle upper characters of different Code Pages
;Some Unicode characters are converted to multiple ASCII characters
;Does handle Big-Endian if first character is Big-Endian "Flag"
;Requires DW 0 to terminate Input String (does not input a Size)
;Intent of program is simply to display SOMETHING on the screen, when
;  possible, to "see" what a UniCode String might be saying.  The conversion
;  is not necessarily complete or accurate, but the representation on
;  the screen should be a reasonable visible approximation of the UniCode
;  string (subject to the limitation forced by the use of 7-bit ASCII
;  characters).  Drops accents and leaves base character for Latin
;  and Latin-like characters.
;I know there are characters that should be translated/displayed that aren't,
;  and vice versa.  There could also be some translations that could be
;  obnoxious or even offensive in certain languages or situations, and
;  I apologize in advance.  I also know there are inconsistencies, where two
;  similar-looking UniCode characters exist, and one is translated and the
;  other isn't.  If you find this to be the case, let me know and I'll update
;  a future version of the program.
;Does not perform function of ANY Control Characters, including CR, LF, Tab.
;  You must preprocess that yourself.
;Write full descriptions for Control Character Acronyms in Docs
;Unwritable characters written {U+xxxx}, xxxx = Hex, others Reserved,
;  Unused, Illegal, Private.  {U-xxxx} means a valid character, but it
;  cannot be closely emulated with 7/8-bit ASCII.
;Visual representations are my judgment, and may not be accurate or even
;  consistent depending on how I was feeling that particular day.


